# v1.6.1

### Added
* Shared Simultaneous sounds (1–16, default 1) and Repeat timeout (ms, default 2000) controls in Event Sounds. Multiple event sounds can play together; when full, the newest alert replaces the oldest. Repeat suppression is keyed by sound file across all events and characters, independent of visual alert duration; 0 disables the timeout and permits overlapping repeats. Changes apply immediately, including lowering the active-sound limit. Manual Test playback stays independent.
* Three sound-volume levels: a shared master control, a shared gain for each saved sound, and a profile-specific gain for each event. The 0–300% levels multiply, default to 100%, support mute and real amplification above 100%, and update playing clips without changing Windows volume. Playback uses Media Foundation streaming and XAudio2 gain, with bounded audio buffers and no changes to the original files. The expanded Event Sounds dialog includes an event assignment checklist with Select all/Clear checks, current sound names, event-volume editing, and one Apply action. Inline notices identify existing assignments that will be replaced without blocking replacements; unchecked events using other sounds are preserved.
* Optional user-selected WAV/MP3 sounds for all monitored events, with compact sound buttons beside event colors, playback tests, and a shared reusable sound library. Browsing adds files to the library automatically; entries can be removed without deleting files or clearing event assignments. Assignments follow event profile overrides, default to silent, and work with event text/border flashes disabled or thumbnails hidden. Asynchronous playback coalesces repeated alerts, releases completed audio files, and logs missing/invalid media without interrupting monitoring. No sound files are bundled.
* Event / Active Border Layout in Thumbnails Visuals: separate event-inside/active-outside rings by default, swapped rings, or the existing combined border. Separate event flashes retain the active/client/group highlight; both layers follow movement, resizing, visibility and cleanup. The test thumbnail demonstrates both borders together. Its button now sits in a separated footer at the very bottom of the Settings sidebar, below the update notice.
* Test Thumbnail button in the Settings sidebar. Opens a temporary thumbnail at the configured default position and size, with current fonts, colors, opacity, custom names, click-through and enabled system/DPS overlays. Configured thumbnail interactions support moving, resizing with minimum-size limits, and sample group/hide/minimize/close actions. Activate-click and middle-click advance samples; automatic states change every second and pause during gestures. Each change rotates Jita, Dodixie, Amarr, Hek, Tama, Turnur and Ahbazon with distinct demo-only system colors, varied incoming/outgoing DPS and damage-type percentages, and configured characters/aliases/colors or varied test names. Temporary geometry and the current sample survive appearance edits. The preview follows effective profile settings and closes with Settings without saving positions or capturing a game client.
* Color pickers for every Settings color field. Click an existing color swatch for thumbnail and event colors, or the picker button beside a custom-color list to update its selected row. The Windows picker opens with the current color; Cancel keeps it unchanged and manual Hex/RGB editing remains available.
* Small hotkey recorder buttons beside every hotkey field, including profile shortcuts, group controls, character rows, Quick Group and non-EVE app bindings. Recording takes place inline with a gray waiting prompt; Esc, clicking the recorder again or moving to another setting cancels. Duplicate-binding indicators show the other assignments and warn about inconsistent behavior without blocking saving or importing.
* Profile activation hotkeys beside the profile selector in Settings. Each profile can have its own shortcut, available from every active profile even without EVE running; activation uses the same save-and-reload action as the tray Profiles menu.
* Shift Logged-In Thumbnails (Unsaved) in Thumbnails Behavior, beside login-screen shifting and enabled by default. Already logged-in characters without a saved thumbnail position use the shared shift direction, spacing, collision avoidance and monitor bounds on startup; saved positions keep priority and the two shifting options can be toggled independently.
* Optional colors for current-system names: characters in the same system share a color, while different occupied systems use different colors. Enable Color System Names by System in Game Logs Monitoring; disabled by default and changes apply immediately.

### Improved
* Master, saved-sound and event volume sliders snap to 5% steps. Their adjacent percentage fields are editable for exact whole percentages, stay synchronized with the sliders, and retain the 0–300% range.
* Monitored Events rows now start with a checkbox and clickable event label. Shortened Stopped Shooting to Shooting idle (ms), with its interval beside the label. Event labels, interval/attack options, colors and square sound buttons use consistent 8px gaps, aligned columns and matching 16px panel margins.
* Window-switching hotkeys automatically gain a wildcard at registration, including character activation, group and Quick Group cycling, previous-window and login-screen cycling, and non-EVE applications. Existing wildcard text is preserved, settings are not rewritten, and duplicate warnings use the effective bindings.
* Settings are saved before a required restart. Profile copies use independent settings and start with an empty activation shortcut; renaming retains current edits and the profile shortcut.
* Game and Local-chat archive scans and startup system lookup run in hidden worker processes so large log folders do not block Settings, tray actions or thumbnail movement. Recent Local matches are published while older headers are still being checked. Local headers are cached between scans; workers use background I/O priority and stop on monitoring shutdown. Live readers process bounded chunks, retain partial lines, and recover recent backlogs without reading whole long-session logs in the UI.
* Thumbnail dragging defers timers until release, caches GUI positions, preserves offsets when moving a group, and skips unchanged mouse positions.
* Game-log discovery shares a newest-session index across characters and refreshes on filename notifications instead of sorting the full archive on every attachment. Quiet sessions remain attached; newer or replaced logs switch after header validation, including after the old log has received updates. Large directory scans yield to mouse/UI handling; slow polling, discovery and diagnostic writes are logged with rate limits.

### Fixed
* Changing Monitored Events with Test Thumbnail open no longer lets mouse callbacks access destroyed windows during a rebuild. Old preview layers are detached before cleanup, and mouse interactions wait until the replacement is ready.
* Removing a saved sound no longer indexes past the shrinking library array. Removing the second sound during preview, any other position, or duplicate entries preserves original files and event assignments.
* Double-border layouts add the inner border's thickness to the configured text margins, including character, event, DPS and system text. Padding stays stable while flashing and does not change saved margins; combined and single-border layouts retain their original spacing. Removed the sidebar footer separator line, keeping the empty space above Test Thumbnail.
* Settings content now starts at the sidebar's measured pixel edge, preventing Windows scaling such as 125% from shifting the panel left underneath the sidebar and clipping labels. Controls retain normal DPI scaling.
* Out-of-memory failures in diagnostics discard temporary log buffers and pause logging for 30 seconds before resuming, avoiding recursive error logging and blocking dialogs. Log appends trim before joining, and access-denied foreground process lookups are treated as untracked windows instead of flooding the log.
* Local-chat discovery workers can replace result and progress snapshots while the UI reads them, avoiding sharing failures that could leave some characters undiscovered.
* Login-screen thumbnail shifting now respects the monitor containing the configured start position, including secondary monitors with negative coordinates. Off-screen start positions use the nearest monitor and are clamped to its bounds, including on first use with collision checking disabled. Corrected shift directions for vertical-first layouts (#9, thanks to @thelonewolfk).
* DWM failures and Windows composition changes now automatically pause live previews and stop further startup attempts until manual Resume. Auto-Pause on DWM Failure in Other is enabled by default and can be disabled without restarting. Interrupted registrations are released, pause cleanup waits for active DWM calls, and About shows the automatic pause reason. Repeated composition notifications are logged once per second.

# v1.6.0

### Added
* Quick Group sorting by added order (default) or character name, selectable in Thumbnails Interactions.
* Configurable hotkeys to pause/resume live previews using the About button action and to exit EVE-X-Preview.
* Always-on bounded program diagnostics, with Show Log and Export Log in About, rotating disk logs, and automatic snapshots on script and DWM errors.
* Pause/Resume Live Previews in About. Pausing unregisters DWM thumbnails while retaining existing hotkeys; resuming respects the selected creation speed.
* Optional Slow Thumbnail Creation in Other, above Switch Language to English on Error. Disabled by default; changing it applies immediately without requiring a restart.
* Diagnostics for settings recovery, activation results, display notifications, runtime DWM/window activity, update checks, and updater download/replacement/relaunch steps.
* Separate Misses options beside Neuts on the compact Player attack and NPC attack rows, enabled by default.
* Automatic background update checks when Settings opens, with a sidebar notice only for newer stable releases. Pre-releases remain available for manual installation in About.
* Incoming and outgoing DPS monitoring with independent thresholds and an adjustable rolling average (default 10 seconds). It shares the game-log reader, monitoring interval and character selection, and works without event alerts enabled.
* Optional incoming EM/thermal/kinetic/explosive damage estimates from bundled drone, missile, fighter and smartbomb profiles, with unknown damage shown separately.
* Custom thumbnail names in Thumbnails Visuals: pair character names with displayed names in two columns, with an Import from Launched button. Names are saved per profile; blank replacements keep the original name.
* Current-system tracking from Local chat logs. The system stays at the bottom of each thumbnail, with active event text above it. Tracking is optional and works independently of combat monitoring.
* Separate Neuts checkboxes for Under Attack By Player and Under Attack By NPC. Incoming energy neutralization is identified by the red GJ amount; outgoing neutralization is ignored. Both options default to off.
* Ignore player smartbomb damage option in Monitored Events, enabled by default.
* Quick Groups, with a custom color, activation hotkey, and an option to exclude their characters from other groups.
* Hotkeys to switch to the previous EVE window, cycle through all logged-in characters, and activate the first launched character in a hotkey group.
* Hide Thumbnail and Quick Group Resets Position options in Thumbnails Interactions.
* Don't Close Disabled Clients and Don't Close Quick Groups Clients options.
* Undocked from NPC Station monitored event. EVE only logs this undocking notification for NPC stations.

### Improved
* With Slow Thumbnail Creation enabled, preview startup and restart wait three seconds, require stable nonzero source dimensions for 500 ms, and process one queued source every 150 ms. Disabled mode creates all ready previews in the current poll. Failed previews retry independently with increasing delays capped at 30 seconds, without permanently stopping recovery or delaying healthy previews.
* Game-log attachment skips unrelated character headers when the character ID is known. If monitoring falls behind by more than 256 KB, it skips to the recent tail and resets DPS totals instead of processing the full backlog.
* Thumbnail updates skip unchanged geometry and visibility, and startup no longer repeatedly shows every existing preview when adding a new one.
* Update checks no longer block the application while waiting for GitHub. Results are cached for five minutes; Check Updates bypasses the cache. Checks time out and report connection errors in About without a popup.
* Expanded general NPC recognition with 6,855 distinct English names from EVE Ref's Entity dataset, covering 7,386 entity types. Name maps are initialized once and reused without runtime downloads.
* New profiles can copy settings from the default profile.
* Corrupted settings recovery: prompts before backing up invalid EVE-X-Preview.json, recreating default settings, and reloading.
* Local chat monitoring reads the latest system on startup, follows new sessions, handles partial writes and UTF-8/UTF-16 logs, and clears the displayed system on logout.
* Update progress is shown in both settings and the updater, with an administrator-rights check before updating.

### Changed

* Release and pre-release installation buttons allow both upgrades and downgrades, and are disabled when the target version equals the installed version, no target is available, or a check is running.
* General NPC detection now uses exact, case-insensitive Map lookups instead of matching name fragments. Faction, officer and capital lists retain their existing names and event priority.
* Thumbnail interactions now use configurable input combinations through OnMessage handling.
* Event messages use a separate bottom text line instead of being appended to the character name. The line moves above the system name when tracking is enabled and uses the existing thumbnail text styling.
* Chat Logs and Game Logs directory settings now share the same layout and automatic detection: leave either field blank or select a custom folder. Detected paths do not fill in the settings fields.

### Fixed
* Profile changes from the tray menu now save atomically before reloading, even when character startup schedules another settings save. Invalid hotkeys caused by a temporary keyboard layout change are retried once in English and logged if still invalid, without restarting the program again.
* Closing a client no longer reports an invalid DWM thumbnail handle as an error when its source or destination window has already closed. Unexpected unregister failures remain logged.
* Client-close cleanup continues for other clients after an individual failure and always re-enables future cleanup. Closed previews are removed from interaction and group maps without redrawing their borders.
* Foreground polling tolerates missing or closed windows during focus changes, clears stale process information, and avoids duplicate diagnostics for already logged timer/message errors.
* Show Log now creates its text control before loading the snapshot, preventing "Can't create control" errors with large diagnostic logs.
* Corrected the DWM visibility/client-area structure offsets, validated DWM results, and released partial thumbnail resources on failures and shutdown.
* Group switching skips active-window retry delays unless a recent activation into that group is still awaiting focus. Preserved logout titles no longer replace the actual foreground window handle.
* Blood Raiders Stronghold is now recognized by its combat-log name, so its neutralizers use the NPC attack option.
* Neuts options now recognize incoming Nosferatu drains (`energy drained to`), including signed GJ amounts, while ignoring capacitor gained (`energy drained from`).
* Fixed FOB NPCs being classified as players when combat logs use Blood Raiders <ship> names instead of diamond-prefixed type names. Added exact aliases for known diamond NPC types, including support for the Guristas <ship> form.
* Check Updates is disabled during an active check, and duplicate requests are suppressed.
* Source builds read the application version for update comparisons instead of falling back to version 1.0.0.0.
* Player names containing NPC name fragments no longer trigger NPC classification.
* Combat-log parsing extracts the entity name from neutralization messages containing both hull and name fields, and correctly identifies targets in missed-shot messages with formatting tags.
* Small thumbnails prioritize the full wrapped character name over event text. Event text is hidden when a complete line cannot fit below the name and returns when space is available.
* Restored thumbnail scaling before first focus (#5, thanks to @ShannaAlabel).
* Monitoring now starts when only attack events are enabled.
* Missing game-log folders allow discovery to retry without opening a folder picker, and changing folders no longer reuses cached paths from the previous directory.

### Other changes
* Added automated update-check coverage for stable-release filtering, version comparison, caching, duplicate requests, timeouts and HTTP errors.
* Moved NPC data into a dedicated NPCDatabase module with a generated name dataset, a PowerShell refresh script and maintenance instructions.
* Added regression coverage for exact NPC matching, player-name collisions, special-event priority, shared maps and combat-log parsing.
* Restore Client Positions is also available in Client Settings, in addition to the tray menu.
* Added Max Active Window Retries and Active Window Retry Interval settings for active-window group detection.
* Added a warning when the settings file comes from a newer configuration version than the program supports.
* The updater now runs from the Windows TEMP folder.
* Added automated coverage for custom names, thumbnail text layout, combat filters, Local chat tracking, and log-directory detection, plus a headless test-runner option.

# v1.5.2

### Changes
* Added Debug Mode functionality for enhanced troubleshooting and runtime inspection.
* Commented out hotkey capture buttons and related logic in settings.
* Improved error handling and expanded debugging output across the entire application.
* Added additional safeguards to detect game lag during cycle execution, with automatic reset of cycle group and index to 1.
* Prevented thumbnail preview images from resetting when “minimize inactive clients” is enabled during character switching.
* Improved monitoring stability, faster initialization, and more reliable file reconnection logic.
* Performed general bug fixes, code cleanup, and performance optimizations.
* Introduced per-character offset when connecting to game log files to reduce lag during multi-character initialization or app reload.
* Fixed an issue where resizing or moving a thumbnail would incorrectly affect the associated game client window.
* Improved settings persistence logic to prevent rare cases of settings file corruption or deletion.
* Unexpected errors now trigger the default AHK error dialog, including class, function, and code context for improved reporting and debugging.
* Updated various settings labels and message popups for clarity and consistency.
* Changed some default settings values.

